   "entry": 11,
   "type": "settlement_re_grade_note",
   "at_utc": "2026-11-16T00:35:00Z",
   "session": "arena/801ba27f-nba1",
   "slate": "2026-11-15",
   "what": "after the parlay-pricing correction (F100) the builder was re-run. It re-graded the 2026-11-15 slate from the same official finals and produced an identical result: 2 graded, 7 pending, +2.00 paper units.",
   "settlement_file_digest_now": "5351e64fb514ae1fa4a2ed8160cc3e8594ea18461405a9c92dc057eede116cb9",
   "matches_entry": 7,
   "settlement_stamp_rule": "settled_at_utc is the moment of the FIRST settlement, not the last builder run. A re-run that grades an identical result keeps the original stamp so the file stays byte-identical and the ledger entry that hashes it remains verifiable; only a genuine change in the graded rows re-stamps it and then a new entry is recorded.",
   "prev": "0136521b5bb18b0a4f3ca0fef590b9bdaad521475d0d1ce192eaf77a9b00b567"
  },
  {
   "entry": 12,
   "type": "correction",
   "at_utc": "2026-11-16T00:52:00Z",
   "session": "arena/801ba27f-nba1",
   "supersedes_entries": [
    6,
    8
   ],
   "superseded_by_entry": 9,
   "defect": "bivariate_normal_cdf() in scripts/build_horizon_801ba27f.py used Simpson weights without the h/3 factor, so every rho-priced joint probability on the parlay and same-game-parlay pages was returned three times too large - the parlay page published joint probabilities above 1.000 (for example 1.6171 for the ORL@BOS / MIL@MIA two-leg).",
   "fix": "the composite Simpson factor h/3 was restored. The corrected function was checked against two closed forms: rho=0 reproduces the independent product exactly (0.670809 for a=0.7, b=1.2) and rho=0.5, a=b=0 reproduces 1/4 + arcsin(rho)/(2*pi) = 0.333333.",
   "effect_on_published_tickets": "no single-leg ticket changes: singles are priced from the normal CDF directly and were never affected. Parlay and SGP joint probabilities were recomputed and re-published as entry 9, still before the tip of the earliest game they cover (2026-11-16). The calibrated example: the ORL@BOS / MIL@MIA two-leg moves from 1.6171 to 0.539 against a naive independent product of 0.5375.",
   "flagged": "F100",
   "note": "the defect is published, not hidden: it is listed on the Flagged for Review page and in the correction row of the parlay-pricing page.",
   "prev": "d5da77038700c08628c9c988b8c713f841d026d8d2b6cb6aa8687f2a92d1da53"
  }
 ],
